# A strict local interaction record in the original spatial family

This research result uses the unchanged family and nonstationary preparation
in `../native_wilson_maxwell_spatial_family/`. Its receipt is
`3e413171f6ad1c0df6cc4db522cb67bc4d9f5f2ae1cfc80d3f4b92fac03538ed`.
The native excitation m, original beta-Wilson rule, fixed spacing a=1/m,
coupling g=1/64, positive complement completion, global code guard, all
old/dual/port/spin references and normalized outer Gauss constraints are
unchanged. The field cap and box size are finite program parameters.
No native complement is deleted. This result does not prepare a
larger-box interacting ground or repair the original dispersion mismatch.
Local support refers to the reconstructed gauge-invariant electric/current
coordinates. The global Foldy-Wouthuysen map and native code guards remain;
no locality theorem on arbitrary microscopic native-complement observables
is asserted.

There is one new bounded, gauge-invariant current detector. After the
three complete code-bank preparation slots, a fair recorded bit chooses
either the physical electric kick `U=exp(i E_e)` or identity on one
interior edge. Every bank then runs under its actual source for
`tau=m t=2^-32`. A final sine-Hadamard detector measures the bounded
unitary `exp(i u J_e)`, `u=2^-16`, where

`F_e=Psi_head^dagger B_e^dagger Psi_tail exp(i g Q_T,e)`,
`J_e=i(F_e-F_e^dagger)`.

All displayed dynamical equations use `H/m` and `tau=m t`. J is its
actual Peierls phase derivative; for the raw source Hamiltonian
`partial_theta H=m J`. The oriented matter charge flow in tau is
`I_e=-J_e` (in physical source time it is `-m J_e`). The electric
equation in tau contains `-g J_e`.
These are source charges and currents, with no electromagnetic or
standard-model identity inferred. The comparison at g=0 uses the same
native code, same Wilson rule, same normalized Gauss carrier, same state
preparation and the same formulas for physical electric/current probes.
It is a mathematical zero-coupling comparison, not a replacement clock
for the actual experiment.

## Exact electric/current interface and all detector outcomes

The physical density is the parent's fixed-frame rho, and
`E_f=P_T,f+g(D G rho_ref)_f`. Exact CAR and cochain identities give

`[rho_x,F_e]=D_ex F_e`,
`[E_f,F_e]=g[(P_T)_fe+(D G D^T)_fe]F_e=g delta_fe F_e`.

Thus the full longitudinal reference is essential: a transverse-only
kick would not shift just the selected link. On the neutral record
sector the root subtraction vanishes; every F and every detector word
preserves total charge. The exact physical intertwiner Y retains the
finite charge labels and all reference states. No sharp continuous
Gauss state is put in a finite member. The unbounded field comparison
uses the same intrinsic reduced algebra/direct-integral construction as
the parent, including its point-fiber continuity, not a normalizable
parent Gauss eigenspace.

In the unbounded comparison,

`U^dagger F_e U=exp(-i g)F_e`,
`[E_f,J_e]=i g delta_fe(F_e+F_e^dagger)`.

The finite-cap source uses literal finite exponentials; the displayed
CCR identity is not asserted on its top occupation boundary. Its
record error is controlled separately below.

Both `||F||<=2` and `||J||<=4` suffice for all bounds. In fact J has
spectrum contained in `{-2,-1,0,1,2}`. Its one-body current has two
eigenvalues +1, two -1 and four zeros: the actual source bond B is a
rank-two partial isometry. Second quantization gives the stated full
eight-mode current spectrum. The literal finite photon phase preserves
this spectrum by a photon-controlled onsite fermion rotation.

The current instrument has Kraus maps

`K_+=(I+i exp(iuJ))/2`, `K_-=(I-i exp(iuJ))/2`.

Their squared effects sum to identity and
`Pr(+)= [1-<sin(uJ)>]/2`. The setting bit, every native code flag,
copied success/failure flag and both detector outcomes are retained.
On code-assembly failure the two observer slots execute recorded no-op
services, with the same elapsed source clock. The physical source
always retains the complete complement; the readout extends as identity
there. The setting-conditioned contrast below does not count distinct
stored setting bits themselves as an influence signal.

## A source-only strictly negative hopping expectation

All integrals here are normalized over the actual bulk Brillouin zone.
In units m=1 the literal original symbol is

`h(q)=alpha.sin(q)+beta[4-cos q_1-cos q_2-cos q_3]`,
`E(q)^2=sum sin^2 q_j+[4-sum cos q_j]^2`.

The source sea projector is `(I-h/E)/2`. For an axis e set
`A=4-cos q_j-cos q_k`, with j,k the other two axes. Its real bare
hopping expectation is

`f=Re<F_e>_matter=integral (A cos q_e-1)/E(q)`.

The imaginary part vanishes by the q -> -q symmetry. In finite open
boxes the actual onsite spin reversal `T=diag(i sigma_2,i sigma_2) K`
preserves every onsite beta and directed B matrix; the free sea
projector is invariant, so the bare hopping expectation is real there
as well. The code checks all three actual bond matrices. Periodic
integration of `partial_qe[sin(q_e)/E(q)]` is legitimate because E>=1.
Using `partial_qe E=A sin(q_e)/E` gives the exact identity

`f=-integral [(A cos q_e-1)^2+sin^2 q_j+sin^2 q_k]/E(q)^3`.

The source identity
`E^2=1+4 sum w_j+2 sum_(j<k)w_j w_k`, `w_j=1-cos q_j`,
gives `E<=7`. The mean of `sin^2 q_j+sin^2 q_k` is one. Therefore

`f<=-1/343`.                                             (1)

This is not a numerical quadrature or a fitted mass. The program
replays the symbolic derivative and polynomial identity directly.

The one-form heat bound in the parent gives a uniform coordinate
variance `v_Q<13`: integrate the unit heat norm bound from 0 to 1 and
the parent's `12/T` covariance tail beyond 1. In the source photon
vacuum the Peierls expectation is `exp(-g^2 v_Q/2)`. Thus the infinite
volume dressed hopping magnitude is greater than

`(1-13/8192)/343 > 1/344`.

There is an explicit finite-box margin as well. The parent's sign
polynomial error bounds the off-diagonal sea-projector difference from
the bulk by `200(99/100)^(J+1)` when the selected edge is farther than
`2J+1` from all faces. Since the trace norm of B is two,

`|f_n-f|<=400(99/100)^(J+1)`.

At J=2048, the exact rational inequality

`[1/343-400(99/100)^2049]*(1-13/8192)>1/345`             (2)

holds. Hence every such interior finite box, as well as its local
limit, has a real photon-dressed hopping expectation at most -1/345.
For example vertices `[-4100,4100]^3` admit the edge from 0 to the
first unit coordinate vector. This enormous witness box is an analytic
sufficient choice, not an executed matrix or an optimal size.

## Uniform short-time control under the full coupled Hamiltonian

Let Omega be the accepted free sea and photon vacuum, with the actual
Gauss reference. The initial physical electric moments obey

`||E_f Omega|| <= 2+2g ||G D_f^T||_2 < 2+52g <3`.

Here the transverse standard deviation is less than 2. The source
Slater variance bound is `||X(a)Omega||<=2||a||_2`, and the proven
Green heat estimate yields
`||G D_f^T||_2 <= sqrt(2)+24 <26` by splitting at heat time one.
Initially `||B_face Omega||<2`. The kick commutes with all E and
shifts each incident B by at most one, so every initial E/B moment
is less than 3 in either setting.

The exact coupled equations on the reducing code are

`dot E=-C^T B-g J`, `dot B=C E`.

Each edge belongs to at most four faces and each face has four edges.
Using the conservative current norm 4, the largest first field moment
M(tau) satisfies

`M(tau) <= (3+g) exp(4|tau|)-g <4`, `|tau|<=1/64`.     (3)

The norm form follows from the strong integrated field equations and
the triangle inequality, not from differentiating an unbounded norm.
Every finite-box free Gaussian/CAR input lies in these first-moment
domains; bounded smooth Peierls terms preserve them. Finite-volume
direct-integral comparison and the displayed uniform bounds justify
the same identities in the intrinsic physical fiber.

For the current commutator, the two onsite matter terms have norm at
most 16 in total, so their contribution is at most 128. At most eleven
hopping edges meet the two endpoints, each with norm at most 4;
their total current-commutator norm is at most 352. Disjoint hoppings
commute in the unbounded comparison. The magnetic energy commutes
with J. The electric quadratic term gives exactly

`i[H_field+H_C,J]=-(g/2){E_e,F_e+F_e^dagger}`.

The same identity includes the Coulomb contribution; omitting it would
leave an incorrect transverse electric force. All scalar baselines,
reference costs and positive completion commute with this neutral code
observable and remain in the autonomous source clock.

To differentiate `sin(uJ)`, the functional-calculus integral also uses
states conjugated by `exp(ivJ)`, with `|v|<=u`. On these states

`||E_e exp(ivJ)psi|| <= ||E_e psi||+4g|v| <5`.

The electric expectation contribution is therefore less than
`4g*5<1`; the bounded matter terms contribute at most 480. Consequently

`|d <sin(uJ(tau))>/d tau| <=512 u`, `|tau|<=1/64`,      (4)

uniformly in box volume and in either kick setting. The functional
calculus argument may first use finite field-domain vectors and then
pass by the first-moment bound. No full operator norm bound on E or
on the unbounded comparison Hamiltonian is asserted.

## Strict complete-record difference

Without the kick the initial current mean is zero. With the kick its
magnitude is `2|<F>| sin g >=g/345`, using `sin g>=g/2` and (2).
For `||J||<=4`,

`||sin(uJ)-uJ||<=64u^3/6`.

The two Taylor allowances and two time-drift allowances imply that
the matched setting-conditioned plus-probability contrast after the
actual autonomous wait is at least

`L=(u/2)[g/345-(64/3)u^2-1024 tau] >0`,               (5)
`g=1/64`, `u=2^-16`, `tau=2^-32`.

The rational producer computes L outward. At g=0, the electric kick
acts only on the photon factor and commutes with the decoupled matter
current at every time. Its contrast is exactly zero.

Let q_n be the full original-attempt code-assembly success probability.
It is the same in the g and g=0 comparisons and is at least the
parent's `1-f_n`. The original unconditioned matched-setting contrast
is at least `q_n L` in the unbounded comparison. For the full law with
the fair setting bit, success/failure and plus/minus outcomes retained,
the total variation distance from its g=0 law is at least `q_n L/2`.
This follows from the triangle inequality between the two Bernoulli
setting rows; it does not count the input bit as an output signal.

The finite-cap and finite-volume allowances below imply that the
limiting complete local law differs strictly from its g=0 comparison
by at least L/2. It is a witnessed interaction in a finite-window
current response of the nonstationary preparation. It is not scattering
from a coupled ground, asymptotic radiation, an interacting continuum
limit, or an assertion about physical particle identity.

## Literal finite caps, local-record convergence and resources

The current detector is a permitted bounded extension of the parent's
local E/B net. Its unitary is the exact interpolation polynomial

`exp(iuJ)=sum_(lambda=-2)^2 exp(iu lambda)`
`                  product_(mu!=lambda)(J-mu)/(lambda-mu)`.

Expanding each J into its two F terms gives at most four Peierls
factors per monomial. The sum of absolute coefficients weighted by
the monomial norm bounds is at most 515. This same polynomial is exact
for every finite cap; no finite Weyl commutation identity is needed.
Every resulting free Dyson word is among the finite mixed
CAR/density/Weyl words controlled in the parent. This proves its
positive-time local record convergence. Initial commutators for this
local bounded current unitary have finite support in the gauge parent,
so the bounded-hopping spatial truncation proof also applies.
Explicitly its initial q commutators vanish, p commutators are at most
`4g u` on the selected edge, and each endpoint CAR-column commutator
is at most `16u`: use `||column Psi||<=2` and
`||exp(iuJ)-I||<=4u`. Thus the parent's spatial estimate has a
concrete volume-independent initial constant and support.

For the finite-cap allowance, add four link radii to the electric-kick
radius: use `s=2+4r`, `r=g sqrt(N/(4sqrt(2)))`, in the parent's
literal-exponential budget. Request ten extra binary digits so that
the factor 515 is absorbed. The actual full-current instrument is
complete, and its operator-polynomial comparison carries every source
complement and pointer outcome. For either coupling setting this
gives `d_n<=2^[-40-2 bit_length(V+1)]`. The zero-coupling comparison
also satisfies this conservative common budget.
More precisely, this is a complete record-law error. Each failed fine
admission pattern has the same probability in both cap comparisons
and has prescribed no-op observer records. Its retained failed source
state may evolve differently; no unproved norm approximation of those
unused complement states is required or asserted. Conditional on any
successful fine pattern the active source factor is exactly the same
free vacuum, so the uniform word bound applies before the fine flags
are marginalized by the local observer.

The original finite-program law therefore has the strict separation

`TV(law_g,n,K,law_0,n,K) >= (1-f_n)L/2-2d_n`          (6)

once the interior margin (2) holds. The producer gives an explicit
finite sufficient box, bank count and total photon cap. Those enormous
native/field matrices are not enumerated. All local outcome laws
converge, since f_n,d_n vanish and the parent finite-word theorem
extends to this finite polynomial current detector.

The elapsed common source time is `5+tau/m`: three native preparation,
admission and routing slots; one recorded kick/identity slot; the
autonomous wait; and one current-readout slot. All branches, unused
banks and retained partners use this same schedule. The five bounded
controls explicitly cancel the raw background during their slots.
Their norm is at most `R B_raw+pi`, and gross switching work at most
`10(R B_raw+pi)`, with the parent's raw, unsubtracted B_raw. These
finite Hermitian-log services are declared programmable apparatus,
not compiled local repair controllers.

Capacity is the parent's R-bank/native/Gauss/photon capacity, plus
`V R ln2` for all cell flags and `3 ln2` for the copied success bit,
fair setting and current outcome. All Gauss-orthogonal and native
complement records remain. Controller coefficient workspace remains
a separate explicit service resource. The photon infinity and spatial
infinity limits are mathematical comparisons of finite record laws;
no finite physical member contains a continuous carrier.
